sequenceDiagram

  actor C as Client
  participant G as Route guard<br/>requireOperation()<br/>ENFORCEMENT POINT 1
  participant H as Route handler<br/>src/routes/requestRoutes.js
  participant S as Service<br/>ENFORCEMENT POINT 2
  participant DB as requestRepository<br/>MongoDB Atlas (DEC-002)
  participant Z as Response serialiser<br/>ENFORCEMENT POINT 3<br/>PLANNED — NOT BUILT
  participant R as src/domain/accessRules.js<br/>the single rule set

  Note over G,R: All three enforcement points evaluate the same rule set.<br/>The rule set is single — the enforcement is distributed — DEC-012.

  alt Path A — refused at the route boundary (function-level access, FR-1.3 / FR-6.4) — implemented and tested
    C->>G: POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/transitions — as a Requester
    G->>R: mayPerformOperation('request:transition', actor)
    R-->>G: false — Requester holds no transition right (FR-1.2 role set)
    G-->>C: 403 — RFC 9457 problem details (DEC-015)
    Note over H,DB: The handler, the service and the database are never reached.<br/>The guard also refuses with 401 when no actor is set, and 403 when<br/>a client supplies an identity in a header (R-06, CON-019).<br/>A route registered without its guard is the failure mode —<br/>the route-table assertion in tests/authorisationGuard.test.js is the NFR-3.3 evidence.

  else Path B — permitted at the boundary, refused in the service (object-level access, FR-4.1 / FR-5.2) — implemented and tested
    C->>G: POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/transitions — as a Technician<br/>If-Match "v3" · Idempotency-Key
    G->>R: mayPerformOperation('request:transition', actor)
    R-->>G: true
    G->>H: next()
    H->>H: readCommand — If-Match (428) and Idempotency-Key (400) required
    H->>S: StatusTransitionService.transition(id, toStatus, actor, command)
    S->>DB: findById(id), inside unitOfWork.run() — DEC-016
    DB-->>S: request document
    S->>R: mayActOnRequest(request, actor)
    R-->>S: false — the request's category is not in the actor's categoryAuthorisations
    S-->>H: AuthorisationError — the transaction aborts, nothing is written
    H-->>C: 403 — RFC 9457 problem details (DEC-015)
    Note over G,S: The boundary could not have made this decision.<br/>The rule depends on the document, which is not loaded<br/>until the service reads it inside the unit of work.<br/>On a security-category request a staff member who is not a<br/>Security Officer is refused here as well (OI-15).<br/>Evidence: tests/statusTransitionService.test.js.

  else Path C — PLANNED, NOT BUILT (blocked on CFL-002) — restricted at the serialiser (field-level access, FR-3.5 / FR-1.5 / NFR-4.4)
    C->>G: GET /api/v1/requests/{id} (planned) — as the Requester who submitted a security-category request
    G->>R: mayPerformOperation('request:read', actor)
    R-->>G: true
    G->>H: next()
    H->>S: request read service (planned — not built)
    S->>DB: findById(id)
    DB-->>S: request document — securityCategory true
    S->>R: mayViewRequest(request, actor)
    R-->>S: true — the requester's own request (FR-3.6)
    S-->>H: request document
    H->>Z: serialise(document, actor)
    Z->>R: visibleStatusFor(status, securityCategory, actor)
    R-->>Z: internal status mapped to Received / In Progress / Closed (FR-3.5)
    Z-->>C: 200 — restricted projection
    Note over S,R: Corrected in this version. The previous drawing showed a staff viewer passing point 2<br/>and being restricted at the serialiser — "reporter identity withheld". The rules forbid that flow:<br/>point 2 refuses every non-Security-Officer staff member on a security-category request (OI-15),<br/>and no requirement restricts the reporter's identity. The requester is the only actor<br/>who reaches point 3 on such a request and is restricted there.<br/>Open — OI-16: does FR-1.5 withhold a requester's own description from them? Read literally it does,<br/>which is almost certainly not intended, and nothing in the requirements settles it.<br/>This path rests on CFL-002, still Proposed — condition C-01 open, exposure RSK-009.
  end
